{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::version` identifies the version of the review rules and the\ncompleted answer's encoding:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Version of these review rules and the result's encoding.\n    /// Change it when an old answer should no longer be reused.\n    fn version(&self) -> CriterionVersion;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nThe {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node`,\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.question_path`, and version identify\nthe same question for checking and execution. Parameters that change which\nquestion is being asked belong in its identity or version.\n\n[Storage](evidence.md#identify-the-saved-assessment) explains how the source node\nand criterion path identify a saved answer and how its version is recorded.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.version`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `Criterion::version` returns a `CriterionVersion` for the review rules and the answer's encoding.\n2. The source node, the criterion path and the version identify the same question for checking and for execution.\n3. A parameter that changes which question is asked belongs in the identity or the version. A changed version means an old answer is not reused.\n4. Storage records the version, as the linked storage section explains. That section is outside this requirement's own text.\n\n**Coverage in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]`**\n- The test `Review` criterion builds its version from its `revision` parameter. This is the \"parameter belongs in the version\" case.\n- Revision `v1` is verified and stored. A reload with `review()` gives a record where `review().version().is_compatible_with(cached.version())` holds. `check_inputs` also passes, so checking and execution agree on the question.\n- A review for a different node, `8`, finds nothing. This covers source-node identity.\n- A review at revision `v2` loads the old record. The test asserts `old.version().as_str() == \"v1\"` and `!v2.version().is_compatible_with(old.version())`. A changed version therefore makes the old answer unreusable.\n- Re-verifying and storing at `v2` replaces the stored version, and the test asserts it is `\"v2\"`.\n- A legacy record with no stored version is still compatible with `CriterionVersion::new(\"v2\")`. This is extra coverage beyond what the text states.\n\n**Coverage in `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]`**\n- This is the production `Review` criterion. It asserts `review().version().as_str() == crate::sdk::REVIEW_VERSION`.\n- After a store and a load through the real graph, it asserts the stored `record.version` equals `REVIEW_VERSION`.\n- It asserts `review().version().is_compatible_with(cached.version())` and that `check_inputs` succeeds.\n- It loads under a different criterion path and gets no record. This covers path identity alongside version.\n\n**Gaps**\nNone found. Both tests carry the `{test}` reference to the subject. Together they check the returned version, version-based reuse and rejection, version recording, and agreement between checking and execution. The \"belongs in identity or version\" clause is covered by the `revision` parameter. The implementation in `src/sdk.rs#fn[review_version]` is a pass-through of a constant.",
