      "definition": "requirements.sdk.application_domain",
      "text": [
        "::::{definition} application_domain",
        ":phrase: application domain",
        "",
        ":::{cite} requirements.sdk.domain",
        "An *application domain* is the application's graph, node contents, and evidence",
        "storage, made available together for criterion execution. In the SDK, it",
        "implements [`Domain`](../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/domain/trait.Domain.html) to supply",
        "its shared types, node and edge operations, and evidence persistence.",
        ":::",
        "::::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "definition": "requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion",
      "text": [
        ":::{definition} criterion",
        ":phrase: criterion",
        "",
        "A *criterion* is a value describing a test to perform on a",
        "{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.node`.",
        "In the SDK, its type implements",
        "[`Criterion<D>`](../../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/graph/trait.Criterion.html) for the",
        "{term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain`. Its",
        "members describe the question's answer, identity, review rules, and execution.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "definition": "requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.question_path",
      "text": [
        ":::{definition} question_path",
        ":phrase: criterion path",
        "",
        "A *criterion path* is an ordered sequence of string segments identifying a",
        "{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion`'s question relative to its",
        "{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node`.",
        "[`CriterionPath`](../../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/graph/struct.CriterionPath.html)",
        "represents this path, while",
        "[`NodeId`](../../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/domain/trait.Domain.html#associatedtype.NodeId)",
        "and its stable",
        "{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_path` identify the source node.",
        "For example, a requirement might use `[\"text\"]`, `[\"behavior\"]`, and",
        "`[\"structure\"]`; a source item's citation checks might use",
        "`[\"citations\", \"requirements.auth.expiration\"]`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "definition": "requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node",
      "text": [
        ":::{definition} source_node",
        ":phrase: source node",
        "",
        "A *source node* is the {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.node` on which a",
        "{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion` is evaluated, identified by",
        "[`Criterion::source_node_id`](../../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/graph/trait.Criterion.html#tymethod.source_node_id).",
        "Tracked reads of its own contents or those of other nodes can supply inputs",
        "without changing the criterion's source node.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "definition": "requirements.sdk.graph.node",
      "text": [
        ":::{definition} node",
        ":phrase: graph node",
        "",
        "A *graph node* is a thing identified in the application's graph, such as a",
        "requirement, a function, a test, or an issue. The application's",
        "[`Domain::NodeId`](../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/domain/trait.Domain.html#associatedtype.NodeId)",
        "identifies it; its contents and the criteria evaluated on it are separate from",
        "that identity.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "definition": "requirements.sdk.graph.node_path",
      "text": [
        ":::{definition} node_path",
        ":phrase: node path",
        "",
        "A *node path* is an ordered sequence of string segments describing a graph",
        "node's identity.",
        "In the SDK, [`NodePath`](../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/graph/struct.NodePath.html)",
        "represents this path.",
        "[`Domain::node_path`](../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/domain/trait.Domain.html#tymethod.node_path)",
        "maps each application-defined",
        "[`NodeId`](../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/domain/trait.Domain.html#associatedtype.NodeId)",
        "to a distinct path that stays stable across runs and changes to the node's",
        "contents.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
